<div class="help-article">
    <p class="help-lead">
        A category says <em>what</em> a transaction was; a tag says what it was <em>for</em>. Tag a rental property's rent,
        repairs, insurance and property tax <em>Rental</em>, or a trip's flights, hotel and meals <em>Vacation</em>, then see
        them together on the dashboard or the transaction list. A transaction can have several tags.
    </p>

    <h3>Tagging transactions</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>One at a time</strong>: <span class="help-ui">+ Tag</span> under a transaction's description, on
            <a href="transactions">Transactions</a> or in the dashboard's transaction panel. Tick tags in the list, or type a new name
            to create it.</li>
        <li><strong>Many at once</strong>: filter Transactions down (search for the property's address or a lender, say), then use
            <span class="help-ui">Tag all … shown</span>. The same menu removes a tag from them all.</li>
        <li><strong>Automatically</strong>: an import gives a transaction the tags on that merchant's newest transaction in the account.</li>
        <li>The × on a tag takes it off.</li>
    </ul>
    <HelpClip Name="tags-tag-all" Caption="Tagging a trip's transactions Vacation, then seeing just those on the dashboard." />

    <h3>Using tags</h3>
    <ul>
        <li>On the <a href="./">Dashboard</a>, pick tags to make every total, chart and list cover only those transactions
            (net worth still covers everything).</li>
        <li>On Transactions, the <strong>Tags</strong> filter does the same for the list.</li>
        <li>On <a href="tags">Tags</a>, each tag's count of transactions links to them.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Managing tags</h3>
    <p>
        Business, Home Office, Moving, Reimbursable, Renovation, Rental, Shared and Vacation are built in. Add your own on the
        <a href="tags">Tags</a> page or from any tag picker, up to 100. Yours can be renamed (they stay on their transactions) or
        deleted (they come off their transactions); the built-in ones can't.
    </p>
    <p class="help-note">
        Tags are for your own grouping. What's claimable on your return is set separately, by each transaction's tax treatment;
        see <a href="help?a=tax-report">Tax report</a>.
    </p>
</div>
